            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Radiotherapy forms a significant part of cancer treatment. Caregivers support and advise patients to help them to adapt to the treatment and limit the occurrence of side effects. A nurse and member of a mobile support care and palliative care unit shares her experience of working in a team using sophrology to relieve the anxiety resulting from the wearing of a mask in radiotherapy.</AbstractText>
